{"name":"Bohemianism","hex":"#b8b3c8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bohemianism","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Bohemian lifestyle.","A word or phrase characteristic of the Bohemian language."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bohemianism"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bohemianism","blocks":[{"text":"Bohemianism is a social and cultural movement that has, at its core, a way of life away from society's conventional norms and expectations. The term originates from the French bohème and spread to the English-speaking world. It was used to describe mid-19th-century non-traditional lifestyles, especially of artists, writers, journalists, musicians, and actors in major European cities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/HemardBohemia1.jpg/330px-HemardBohemia1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bohemianism"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Bohemian_Grove_during_the_summer_Hi-Jinks%2C_circa_1911-16..jpg/500px-Bohemian_Grove_during_the_summer_Hi-Jinks%2C_circa_1911-16..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Bohemian_Grove_during_the_summer_Hi-Jinks%2C_circa_1911-16..jpg/500px-Bohemian_Grove_during_the_summer_Hi-Jinks%2C_circa_1911-16..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bohemian Grove during the summer Hi-Jinks, circa 1911–1916","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABohemian_Grove_during_the_summer_Hi-Jinks%2C_circa_1911-16..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Bohemian_Life_%281899%29_%2814785593483%29.jpg/500px-Bohemian_Life_%281899%29_%2814785593483%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8